WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.870
Both my wife and I have been wearing an Apple
Watch Series 4 on our wrists for the past

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.810
2 months, and I’ve noticed a few things
that really put into perspective who should

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.019
be buying an Apple Watch, and which Apple
Watch they should be buying.

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:14.880
During Apple’s September Event, I found
myself drooling over many of the Apple Watch

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.810
Series 4’s new features, like the larger
rounded display, all the new fullscreen watch

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:25.599
faces, the redesigned crown, the louder speaker,
the beautifully redesigned back, and more.

00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:28.470
Over the past 2 months, I’ve found that
a lot of that stuff doesn’t really matter

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.470
to me anymore.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:33.860
I consider myself more of a casual user since
my phone is no more than a foot away from

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.250
me at all times, so I find myself picking
up my phone to reply to messages instead of

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.500
just using the watch.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.340
I’ve realized that I’m not alone in that
regard.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.160
There are a lot of people who don’t use
the Apple Watch to its full potential, which

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.610
makes me question why they bought one in the
first place.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.780
And it goes even further when you think about
why they bought the Series 4 instead of the

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.830
Series 3.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:56.430
My wife, on the other hand, has benefitted
greatly from her Apple Watch.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:00.260
She runs a business in the services industry
so she’s constantly getting phone calls

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.650
and notifications.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:05.410
Before the Apple Watch, she used to miss calls
all the time and not reply to messages from

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.950
clients for over an hour sometimes.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:13.070
Now, she can instantly reply to messages and
answer phone calls using her connected AirPods,

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.640
all without ever touching or even looking
at her phone.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.900
So if you’re someone who runs a business
and you struggle with missed phone calls and

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.120
messages that you don’t notice for hours,
the Apple Watch will bring you immense amounts

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.120
of value.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.120
Like my wife, a lot of girls carry their phones
in their purses and end up missing out on

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.120
phone calls and notifications, so it’s even
more of a value for girls.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.120
So based on those reasons, she can’t leave
the house, or even the charging dock, without

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.120
it.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.120
Now if you’re like me and your phone is
always in your pocket or at least a foot away

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.030
from you at all times, you won’t reap as
many benefits, but there’s still a lot to

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.300
love about the Apple Watch.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.420
I found that there are generally two main
reasons to buy an Apple Watch.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:39.620
#1 is as a fashion piece, and #2 is for the
actual functionality.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:43.640
When it comes down to it, the Series 3 is
a beautifully designed Apple Watch, just like

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.880
the Series 4, therefore satisfying most of
the fashion statement piece of it.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.350
Of course, there are also those who buy the
latest model for the fashion side of it as

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.350
well.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.580
As for functionality, I’ve realized that
the Series 3 can do almost everything that

00:01:55.580 --> 00:02:00.120
the Series 4 can do, and a big part of that
is health and fitness tracking, which it does

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.980
basically just as well as the Series 4, at
least what you’d notice.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:08.030
On top of that, the Series 3 supports of all
the same great features that came with watchOS

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.030
5.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.329
I’ve personally noticed that most of the
improvements that come with the Series 4 are

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:15.939
actually luxury improvements that you don’t
really need but will make your experience

00:02:15.939 --> 00:02:16.940
a little bit better.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:20.799
For example, the larger rounded display is
nice to have, but you don’t really need

00:02:20.799 --> 00:02:21.799
it.

00:02:21.799 --> 00:02:24.019
The louder speaker is nice, but you’ll be
fine without it.

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:28.609
The S4 processing chip is definitely faster,
but the Series 3 already felt fast enough

00:02:28.609 --> 00:02:29.859
almost all the time.

00:02:29.859 --> 00:02:33.189
The older-gen sensors worked just fine on
the Series 3.

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:36.799
The new back on the Series 4 is nice, but
you’ll only see it when you take your watch

00:02:36.799 --> 00:02:37.799
off to charge.

00:02:37.799 --> 00:02:40.739
The new crown is a lot better, but the old
crown works just fine.

00:02:40.739 --> 00:02:41.739
You get the point.

00:02:41.739 --> 00:02:46.450
The Series 3 was able to achieve almost everything
that the Series 4 could, albeit not as well,

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.260
or not as luxurious-feeling.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:53.239
The issue with that is that the Series 4 starts
at $400, while the Series 3 starts at $279

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:57.249
and is more likely to be on sale in stores
as well.

00:02:57.249 --> 00:03:00.739
With that large of a price gap, are people
really willing to pay that much extra for

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:01.739
luxury improvements?

00:03:01.739 --> 00:03:02.739
Well, yes.

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:05.500
That’s why there are people who upgrade
their iPhones every year.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.060
The reason I purchased a Series 4 over a Series
3 is that I’m the type of the guy who will

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:14.099
never buy an older model of a device when
a new one was just released, whether it’s

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:15.639
an iPhone or a MacBook, I won’t buy an older
model, even to save a good chunk of cash.

00:03:15.639 --> 00:03:19.400
In the last 2 months of using the Series 4,
here are the features that actually made a

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.989
difference in day-to-day use.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:23.709
The most important one is the Chronograph
watch face.

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:27.980
I absolutely love that I can have up to 8
different complications on the screen, giving

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.029
me all the information I need with just a
glance.

00:03:31.029 --> 00:03:32.409
Another one is the digital crown.

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:36.560
It’s hard to explain but it feels and functions
so much better than the old crown.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.790
The Series 4 is also incredibly quick, but
the difference while using the UI is small,

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:44.069
so you’ll never know it unless you go from
a Series 4 to a 3.

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:46.819
I’ve also noticed a significant improvement
in battery life.

00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:51.340
I usually charge it every single night, but
when I forget, it lasts the entire second

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.319
day and it’ll still have some left over
by the time I go to bed.

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:55.319
And that’s about it.

00:03:55.319 --> 00:03:58.790
Those are the changes that actually made a
difference in day-to-day use.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.120
Everything else comes down to watchOS 5 improvements,
which the Series 3 also supports.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.560
So if the Series 3 can satisfy both the fashion
statement and functionality pieces of the

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.059
puzzle, who should buy the Series 4?

00:04:10.059 --> 00:04:13.150
Basically, anyone who doesn’t mind throwing
down some extra cash to make sure they have

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.579
the latest and greatest Apple Watch out there,
while also enjoying some of those extra luxury

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:18.680
improvements.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:22.330
Other than that, the Series 4 also features
some new health and safety features like fall

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:27.310
detection and the ability to take an electrocardiogram,
which is more than enough reason to go with

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.310
the Series 4 if you’re worried about health.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.319
Here’s another thought.

00:04:30.319 --> 00:04:33.550
A lot of people don’t really need an Apple
Watch, but they want one.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.419
This means that lots of Apple Watches are
purchased as gifts, and if you’re buying

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:41.949
it as a gift, the $279 Apple Watch Series
3 is going to look a lot more attractive to

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:42.949
you.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.770
You’ll save quite a bit of cash and it’s
still going to put a huge smile on their face.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.759
And I don’t see anything wrong with that.

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:51.509
The Series 3 will more than get the job done,
so if you’re shopping for someone else,

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:55.889
just buy a Series 3 unless they specifically
showed a lot of interest in the Series 4.

00:04:55.889 --> 00:04:59.729
Now if you’re thinking about buying yourself
an Apple Watch, after spending two months

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:03.729
with my Series 4, I honestly think that you’ll
be perfectly happy with the Series 3.

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:07.361
Now if you don’t mind spending some more
cash, then definitely buy the Series 4 for

00:05:07.361 --> 00:05:14.389
all of the luxury improvements and added features.

